<p>This blog is a collection of questions, ideas, and mysteries that I don’t know (yet) and I wish to get answered before I die.</p>

<strong>Philosophy</strong>
<ul>
  <li>What is life and what is the purpose of it, and why do we even exist?</li>
  <li>Does God exist?</li>
  <li>Fate and free will</li>
  <li>Are humans inherently good or evil? Are people born evil?</li>
  <li>What’s right and wrong? What's fair and unfair?</li>
  <li>Is morality subjective?</li>
  <li>Is it about the journey/process or the destination/outcome?</li>
  <li>What happens after we die?</li>
</ul>

<strong>Mind & Perception</strong>
<ul>
  <li>What is consciousness?</li>
  <li>How does the mind relate to the body, and can consciousness exist independently of it?</li>
  <li>How can I know that other people are real and truly conscious, and not just illusions, projections, or creations of my imagination?</li>
  <li>Ship of Theseus: what makes an object the same over time?</li>
  <li>Perception of color and subjective reality</li>
  <li>Why do we dream?</li>
  <li>What causes déjà vu?</li>
  <li>Why do some people experience tinnitus?</li>
</ul>

<strong>Physics</strong>
<ul>
  <li>What is before the Big Bang?</li>
  <li>What is beyond the edge of the universe?</li>
  <li>What is dark matter and dark energy?</li>
  <li>Is there a multiverse?</li>
  <li>Does alien life exist?</li>
  <li>Black hole and singularity</li>
  <li>Can we time travel to the past? (Grandfather Paradox)</li>
  <li>What are the cosmological consequences once the universe reaches a state of maximum entropy and achieves global thermodynamic equilibrium?</li>
  <li>Quantum entanglement</li>
</ul>

